--[[
        NEW SEEK -- DOORS' Seek with another body, and its glitched version

            _G.Type = "Normal"   -- or "Glitch"
            loadstring(game:HttpGet("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bonellocristian78-lab/Gradish-Mode/claude/sei-qui-con-noi-ye4k62/NewSeek"))()

        Every Seek that comes (SeekMovingNewClone, SeekMoving) wears the new one: DOORS' own is still there (the server
        moves it, its hit and its cutscenes are its own) but you see the new one in its place. Each part of the new one's
        body goes where DOORS' part of the same name is, every frame (out of the floor, the run). If DOORS' Seek has not
        those parts, the new one follows it whole and plays DOORS' joints, or its own animations (emerge, run, idle).
        DOORS' own is hidden only once the new one is in its place. What it found and how it follows it is written in
        NewSeek/SeekStructure.txt (and the console, F9).

        Glitch: Seek made of DOORS' Glitch (ReplicatedStorage.Entities.Glitch). Its purple body, glowing, under Glitch's
        cube texture, Glitch's cube particles (white, red, cyan), Glitch's pink light. Its eyes are glitched: a glowing
        cube of Glitch's on each, flickering pink, cyan and white, and their faces swap between Seek's eye and the cube.
        Its hands are clusters of glowing cubes that never keep still. Cubes break off
        it all the time, its colours flicker, its limbs jump off their joints, it hangs a moment and snaps on, its
        sounds warble, and when it is close Glitch's cubes flash on your screen.

        Light on the game: nothing is made while it runs (its cubes are always the same few, moved), DOORS' Seek is
        hidden once (not every frame), no shadows from it, fewer goo particles.

        Only you see it. Run it again to change type; getgenv().__NewSeek() takes it off.
        Its model is assets/seek/NewSeek.rbxm, downloaded once into the executor's folder (NewSeek/).
]]

